#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# discrete_max_limit

#% text
# `discrete_max_limit(f, k -> inf)` gives the upper limit of the sequence f(k) as the integer k grows; `k -> -inf` as it decreases.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# With a period P of the oscillating factors (powers of negative numbers, sin and cos of rational multiples of pi k) the value is the largest of the limits along the residues k = r (mod P). When an angle is not a rational multiple of pi the values are dense and `max_limit` over the reals is used.

#% item
# Lists are handled element-wise.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
discrete_max_limit((-1)^k, k -> inf)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
discrete_max_limit((3 + (24/25)^k)*sin(pi*k/20), k -> inf)
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
discrete_max_limit(sin(k), k -> inf)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
discrete_max_limit((-1)^k*3*k/(1 + 6*k), k -> inf)
#% output
#= 1/2

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `discrete_min_limit`, `max_limit`, `discrete_limit`
